1c:["$","$1b","0",{"children":[["$","$1b","0",{"children":[["$","p","0",{"children":["A useful test starts with a narrower decision, such as whether two feasible windows differ for one account and one recurring format. Assign comparable planned posts across those windows before publishing, keep the observation period fixed, and record exceptions rather than quietly replacing them. Repeat across enough independent occasions to avoid building a schedule around one lucky day. If the audience spans time zones, document whose clock you mean. The result can inform this operation under these conditions; it is not a universal calendar of when the internet is receptive."]}]]}]]}]
